# LF in the repository and in a checkout, on every platform.
#
# Three files had drifted to CRLF while the other sixty-six were LF:
# `.github/workflows/ci.yml`, the claim registry entry, and
# `kernel/src/mem.rs`. The last of those turned a two-line `cargo fmt` change
# into an 824-line diff, which is the cost being paid here — a line ending that
# depends on who last saved a file is charged to every diff after it, not just
# the one that introduced it.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Except an import, which is upstream's bytes and not this tree's text. A data
# import is checked by SHA-256 against its PROVENANCE.md (RFC 0114), so a
# checkout that normalised one line ending in one imported file would make
# `lint-licensing` red on a machine whose only difference is its git settings —
# and, worse, would make the file this tree tests against not the file upstream
# published. `-text` means git never converts it, in either direction.
#
# *What would reverse this:* nothing that is an import; an authored file under
# third_party/ (a README, a PROVENANCE.md) is LF already and loses nothing.
third_party/** -text
